<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Cerretani</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 150 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Pyrenean people of Cerdanya, famed in Roman times for their hams, whose name lives on in the Cerdanya valley.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Cerretani occupied the high Pyrenean valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segre">Segre</a>, today divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/andorra">Andorra</a>. They probably spoke an Iberian language, and are recorded from the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pastoralism">pastoralism</a> and farming in the mountains, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> noted that their hams were highly prized and profitable. Little is known of their political organisation. Their valley controlled routes across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> basin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They came under Roman control in the 2nd century BCE as part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a> names the Roman town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llivia">Iulia Libica</a>, modern Llívia, in their territory, and the name of the people survives in the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cerretani.jpg" alt="Cerretani" width="320" height="527"><figcaption>Image: si.robi · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cerretani_RG18_(9)_(42260494474).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 150 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Iberian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a>, <a href="/countries/andorra">Andorra</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ceretani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-325&amp;focus=cerretani" aria-label="Cerretani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4600 761 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cerretani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4920 1017h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4920 1017h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=-325&amp;focus=cerretani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
